++
++<h1>PRD: Messaging Offline Availability — Content Cards, CBE &amp; Inbox (iOS SDK)</h1>
++
++<h2>1. Executive summary</h2>
++<h3>Problem</h3>
++<p>Content Cards, Code-Based Experiences (CBE), and Inbox feeds today live <strong>primarily in memory</strong>. After app restart or offline use, surfaces are empty until the next successful network fetch. In-App Messages already persist to device and reload on cold start. Customers (e.g. Disney — poor park Wi‑Fi) need messaging content from the <strong>last good online session</strong> available offline.</p>
++
++<h3>Proposed solution</h3>
++<p>Persist eligible proposition rules to device after every <strong>successful</strong> <code>updatePropositionsForSurfaces</code>. On read, the SDK uses a <strong>memory-first, disk-second</strong> strategy — no integrator flag required. Whether a proposition is eligible for disk persistence is controlled by an <strong>authoring-side offline availability flag</strong> delivered in the Edge payload (<code>scopeDetails.characteristics.mobileParameters.offline</code>), with UI placement TBD (see §5.5).</p>
++
++<h3>Scope expansion (2026-07-14)</h3>
++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
++<tr><th>Surface type</th><th>Schemas</th><th>Offline persistence</th><th>Read APIs</th></tr>
++<tr><td><strong>Content Cards</strong></td><td><code>.feed</code>, <code>.contentCard</code></td><td>Proposed ✅ (gated by <code>offlineAvailable</code>)</td><td><code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code>, <code>getContentCardsUI</code></td></tr>
++<tr><td><strong>Code-Based Experiences</strong></td><td><code>.jsonContent</code>, <code>.htmlContent</code>, <code>.defaultContent</code></td><td>Proposed ✅ (gated by <code>offlineAvailable</code>)</td><td><code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code></td></tr>
++<tr><td><strong>Inbox</strong></td><td><code>.inbox</code> container-item + linked CC propositions</td><td>Proposed ✅ (container + cards; see callouts)</td><td><code>getInboxUI</code> → internal get/update</td></tr>
++<tr><td><strong>In-App Messages</strong></td><td>IAM rulesets</td><td>Existing (unchanged)</td><td>Automatic on launch</td></tr>
++</tbody></table>
++
++<h3>Key decisions</h3>
++<ul>
++<li><strong>No integrator read flag</strong> — SDK auto-hydrates from disk when in-memory data is missing or empty for requested surfaces.</li>
++<li><strong>Memory-first read order</strong> — always consult session memory before disk.</li>
++<li><strong>Separate disk keys per surface family</strong> — <code>contentCardPropositions</code>, <code>codeBasedPropositions</code>, <code>inboxPropositions</code> (IAM remains <code>propositions</code>).</li>
++<li><strong>Save rules, not UI</strong> — store Adobe rules; re-run qualification on read so dismiss/expiry still apply.</li>
++<li><strong>Authoring gate</strong> — SDK only persists propositions where server sets <code>offlineAvailable: true</code> (defaults <code>true</code> when absent for backward compatibility).</li>
++<li><strong>Failed fetch protection</strong> — offline/timeout stream close must not mutate any persisted store.</li>
++<li><strong>Clear on logout</strong> — <code>resetIdentities</code> wipes CC/CBE/Inbox memory + disk (<a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-62504">PLATIR-62504</a>).</li>
++</ul>
++
++<h3>Top risks</h3>
++<ul>
++<li>Authoring flag placement undecided → payload contract may shift.</li>
++<li>Offline read latency up to <strong>5 seconds</strong> in current design when reads are queued behind network updates (see Callout §6.1).</li>
++<li>Inbox requires <strong>both</strong> container-item and card propositions — partial persistence shows error UI.</li>
++<li>Images may not render offline (lazy cache — <a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-44800">PLATIR-44800</a>).</li>
++<li>Dismissed cards may briefly reappear on cold start until event history catches up (Option B disk eviction open).</li>
++</ul>
++
++<h2>2. Context and problem statement</h2>
++<h3>2.1 Current behavior (as-is)</h3>
++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
++<tr><th>Action</th><th>Content Cards / CBE / Inbox today</th></tr>
++<tr><td>Successful online update</td><td>Propositions in memory for this session</td></tr>
++<tr><td>App killed / cold start</td><td>Memory gone → empty until network</td></tr>
++<tr><td>Offline</td><td>Empty (unless same-session memory)</td></tr>
++<tr><td>Logout</td><td>CC cache not cleared → cross-user risk (<a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-62504">PLATIR-62504</a>)</td></tr>
++</tbody></table>
++
++<h3>2.2 Customer use case — Disney</h3>
++<p>In the park, network is often poor. The app needs cards and inbox content available offline and interactive. When online, only deltas should go over the wire. Multiple business units compete for bandwidth — messaging surfaces should not require a fresh fetch on every screen open.</p>
++
++<h3>2.3 PLATIR drivers</h3>
++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
++<tr><th>Ticket</th><th>Problem</th><th>Required response</th></tr>
++<tr><td><a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-62504">PLATIR-62504</a></td><td>Cross-user card leakage on shared devices</td><td>Clear CC/CBE/Inbox cache on <code>resetIdentities</code></td></tr>
++<tr><td><a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-54423">PLATIR-54423</a></td><td>Stale cache when server stops sending a feed</td><td>Remove feeds requested but not returned on successful update</td></tr>
++<tr><td><a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-44800">PLATIR-44800</a></td><td>Offline broken images (IAM)</td><td>CC/CBE images lazy — open for product</td></tr>
++<tr><td><a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-64717">PLATIR-64717</a></td><td>Empty <code>items[]</code> proposition shells</td><td>Do not persist empty shells (open)</td></tr>
++</tbody></table>
++
++<h2>3. Goals and non-goals</h2>
++<h3>3.1 Goals</h3>
++<ul>
++<li>G1 — Persist eligible proposition rules after successful online fetch (CC, CBE, Inbox).</li>
++<li>G2 — SDK reads saved content offline via automatic memory-first + disk hydrate (no app flag).</li>
++<li>G3 — Authoring controls per-proposition offline eligibility via server payload.</li>
++<li>G4 — No cross-user leakage on shared devices after logout.</li>
++<li>G5 — Evict stale feeds when server returns nothing for a requested surface (successful update only).</li>
++<li>G6 — Same read semantics across <code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code>, <code>getContentCardsUI</code>, and <code>getInboxUI</code> internal reads.</li>
++</ul>
++
++<h3>3.2 Non-goals (this PRD)</h3>
++<ul>
++<li>Android / React Native wrapper exposure (follows iOS).</li>
++<li>Proactive image/asset prefetch for offline (<a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-44800">PLATIR-44800</a>).</li>
++<li>Public <code>clearCachedContentCardPropositions()</code> API (backlog).</li>
++<li>Detailed engineering file-level implementation (see repo <code>docs/agents/</code>).</li>
++</ul>
++
++<h2>4. Requirements</h2>
++<h3>4.1 Functional requirements</h3>
++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
++<tr><th>ID</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
++<tr><td>FR-1</td><td>On successful <code>updatePropositionsForSurfaces</code>, persist eligible rules to separate disk keys per surface family</td></tr>
++<tr><td>FR-2</td><td>On failed/timeout update (zero <code>personalization:decisions</code>), do <strong>not</strong> change phone cache</td></tr>
++<tr><td>FR-3</td><td><code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code> returns in-memory data when present; otherwise hydrates from disk automatically</td></tr>
++<tr><td>FR-4</td><td><code>getContentCardsUI</code> uses same read path as get propositions (no separate flag)</td></tr>
++<tr><td>FR-5</td><td><code>getInboxUI</code> benefits from same persistence model for inbox surface (container-item + linked cards)</td></tr>
++<tr><td>FR-6</td><td>SDK persist gate: only propositions with <code>offlineAvailable == true</code> written to disk</td></tr>
++<tr><td>FR-7</td><td>Requested surface absent from successful server response → remove that surface from relevant disk key</td></tr>
++<tr><td>FR-8</td><td>Surfaces not part of current update request → leave disk cache unchanged</td></tr>
++<tr><td>FR-9</td><td><code>resetIdentities</code> clears CC/CBE/Inbox memory + disk; IAM disk unchanged</td></tr>
++</tbody></table>
++
++<h3>4.2 Non-functional requirements</h3>
++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
++<tr><th>ID</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
++<tr><td>NFR-1</td><td><strong>Backward compatibility</strong> — payloads without <code>offline</code> flag default to persist (<code>true</code>)</td></tr>
++<tr><td>NFR-2</td><td><strong>Identity safety</strong> — no prior user's content after logout/login</td></tr>
++<tr><td>NFR-3</td><td><strong>Read latency</strong> — disk hydrate should complete in &lt;200ms when not blocked by queue (target; see callouts)</td></tr>
++<tr><td>NFR-4</td><td><strong>Observability</strong> — consider Assurance event when content served from disk (open)</td></tr>
++</tbody></table>
++
++<h2>5. Solution design</h2>
++
++<h3>5.1 High-level architecture</h3>
++<p>End-to-end flow from authoring → server → SDK gates → app APIs.</p>
++
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="arch-flow-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">text</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">Server → SDK → App (proposed)</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[
++┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
++│  AJO AUTHORING (placement TBD — see §5.5)                                   │
++│  Sets "Offline availability" → serialized into Edge proposition payload    │
++└──────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘
++                                   │ personalization:decisions (Edge stream)
++                                   ▼
++┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
++│  SERVER PAYLOAD                                                              │
++│  Proposition.scopeDetails.characteristics.mobileParameters.offline: Bool     │
++│  (defaults true when absent)                                                 │
++└──────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘
++                                   │
++          ┌────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┐
++          │ WRITE PATH (online)                            │ READ PATH (anytime)
++          ▼                                                ▼
++┌──────────────────────────┐              ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
++│ updatePropositions       │              │ getPropositionsForSurfaces       │
++│ ForSurfaces              │              │ getContentCardsUI                │
++│                          │              │ getInboxUI (internal get)        │
++│ 1. Edge stream           │              │                                  │
++│ 2. Success guard         │              │ 1. Check IN-MEMORY cache  ◄──────┼── FIRST
++│    (≥1 decisions event)  │              │ 2. If nil/empty → DISK hydrate │
++│ 3. ParsedPropositions    │              │ 3. Run rules engine            │
++│    schema routing:       │              │ 4. Return propositions / UI    │
++│    • CC  → cc key        │              └──────────────────────────────────┘
++│    • CBE → cbe key       │
++│    • Inbox → inbox key   │
++│ 4. SDK GATE:             │
++│    if offlineAvailable   │
++│    → write disk          │
++│ 5. Update memory         │
++└──────────────────────────┘
++]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h3>5.2 AJO Inbox surface model</h3>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="inbox-model-001"><ac:rich-text-body>
++<p><strong>Important:</strong> AJO authors assign cards a primary surface (<code>s1</code>, <code>s2</code>) and an inbox surface (<code>i1</code>) via <code>inboxSurfaces</code>. IDS remaps the response scope to <code>i1</code>. The SDK <strong>only sees <code>i1</code></strong>.</p>
++<p>A single <code>updatePropositionsForSurfaces([i1])</code> returns the inbox container-item <strong>and</strong> all linked content cards, all scoped to <code>i1</code>. No separate surface requests needed.</p>
++</ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h3>5.3 Data storage (logical)</h3>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="storage-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">text</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Cache file:  com.adobe.messaging.cache
++
++Keys (separate, never shared):
++  propositions              → In-App Messages (existing)
++  contentCardPropositions   → Content Cards / feeds
++  codeBasedPropositions     → CBE (json/html/default content)
++  inboxPropositions         → Inbox container-item schema
++
++Format:  JSON { "surfaceUri": [ Proposition, ... ] }
++What we save: Adobe RULES — not final UI models]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h3>5.4 API contract &amp; integration patterns</h3>
++
++<h4>updatePropositionsForSurfaces — network write</h4>
++<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Fetch fresh propositions from Edge; on success, update memory and persist eligible rules to disk.</p>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="api-update-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">swift</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Messaging.updatePropositionsForSurfacesWithCompletionHandler([surface]) { success in
++    // success == true  → stream completed AND ≥1 personalization:decisions received
++    // success == false → timeout, invalid surfaces, or zero decisions (disk UNCHANGED)
++}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h4>getPropositionsForSurfaces — memory-first read</h4>
++<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Host apps rendering custom UI (CBE JSON/HTML, custom card feeds, diagnostics).</p>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="api-get-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">swift</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Messaging.getPropositionsForSurfaces([surface]) { propositionsBySurface, error in
++    // 1. Returns in-memory qualified propositions when available
++    // 2. Auto-hydrates from disk when memory is nil/empty for requested surface
++    // 3. Empty result → [] with error == nil
++}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h4>getContentCardsUI — templated card UI</h4>
++<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Apps using Adobe Content Card UI components. Internally calls <code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code> — same memory-first + disk hydrate semantics.</p>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="api-ccui-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">swift</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Messaging.getContentCardsUI(for: surface,
++                              customizer: customizer,
++                              listener: listener) { result in
++    // Builds ContentCardUI models from propositions returned by get path
++}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h4>getInboxUI — inbox container + cards</h4>
++<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Adobe Inbox UI. Requires <strong>both</strong> inbox container-item proposition and content card propositions for the same inbox surface.</p>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="warning" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="inbox-dep-001"><ac:rich-text-body>
++<p>If only cards are cached but the inbox container-item is missing, <code>InboxUI</code> shows an error state — even when card data exists on disk. Both must persist for offline inbox.</p>
++</ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="api-inbox-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">swift</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Messaging.getInboxUI(for: inboxSurface, ...) { result in
++    // Internally: updatePropositions → getPropositions
++    // Once disk hydration is active, offline get can still succeed if both
++    // container-item and cards were previously persisted
++}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h4>Recommended integration pattern (cache-first)</h4>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="pattern-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">swift</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">Show cached content immediately; refresh in background</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[// 1. Read local first (memory → disk auto-hydrate)
++Messaging.getContentCardsUI(for: surface) { result in
++    showCards(result)  // instant when cache exists
++}
++
++// 2. Background network refresh (do not block step 1)
++Messaging.updatePropositionsForSurfacesWithCompletionHandler([surface]) { success in
++    if success {
++        Messaging.getContentCardsUI(for: surface) { result in showCards(result) }
++    }
++}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h3>5.5 Authoring-side offline flag — three placement options (OPEN)</h3>
++<p>The SDK reads <code>scopeDetails.characteristics.mobileParameters.offline</code> from the Edge proposition. <strong>Where authors set this in AJO UI is not yet decided.</strong> Three options under discussion:</p>
++
++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
++<tr><th>Option</th><th>Placement</th><th>Granularity</th><th>Trade-offs</th></tr>
++<tr><td><strong>Option 1</strong></td><td>Channel configuration (Content Cards channel)</td><td>Per channel / surface path</td><td>Simple for marketers; all cards on a surface share same offline policy</td></tr>
++<tr><td><strong>Option 2</strong></td><td>Content editor (per card / message)</td><td>Per individual content card</td><td>Fine-grained control; authors decide card-by-card</td></tr>
++<tr><td><strong>Option 3</strong></td><td>Global launch configuration</td><td>App-wide checkboxes (CC offline, CBE offline, Inbox offline, …)</td><td>Centralized policy; less per-message flexibility</td></tr>
++</tbody></table>
++
++<p><strong>Option 1 — Channel configuration</strong> (surface/path level):</p>
++<p><ac:image ac:align="center" ac:alt="Offline availability at channel config"><ri:attachment ri:filename="offline-flag-channel-config.png" /></ac:image></p>
++
++<p><strong>Option 2 — Content editor</strong> (per card):</p>
++<p><ac:image ac:align="center" ac:alt="Offline availability in content editor"><ri:attachment ri:filename="offline-flag-content-editor.png" /></ac:image></p>
++
++<p><strong>Option 3 — Global launch config</strong> (not mocked): checkbox list at campaign launch — e.g. "Offline availability of Content Cards", "Offline availability of CBE", "Offline availability of Inbox". Applies uniformly to all content in that launch.</p>
++
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="note" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="authoring-open-001"><ac:rich-text-body>
++<p><strong>Open question:</strong> Product must confirm which option (or combination) ships. SDK defaults <code>offlineAvailable = true</code> when flag absent so existing campaigns continue to persist until authoring UI ships.</p>
++</ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h3>5.6 Comparison to In-App Messages</h3>
++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
++<tr><th>Topic</th><th>IAM</th><th>CC / CBE / Inbox (this PRD)</th></tr>
++<tr><td>Save after online fetch</td><td>Yes — <code>propositions</code></td><td>Yes — separate keys per family</td></tr>
++<tr><td>Authoring offline gate</td><td>N/A today</td><td><code>mobileParameters.offline</code> (proposed)</td></tr>
++<tr><td>Load on read</td><td>Auto on app launch</td><td>Memory-first; disk hydrate when empty</td></tr>
++<tr><td>Integrator flag</td><td>None</td><td>None (removed from earlier design)</td></tr>
++<tr><td>Clear on <code>resetIdentities</code></td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
++</tbody></table>
++
++<h2>6. Callouts &amp; open questions</h2>
++<p>This section captures product decisions, known behaviors, and unresolved questions. <strong>Not implementation detail.</strong></p>
++
++<h3>6.1 Callout — Offline content may take up to 5 seconds to appear</h3>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="warning" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="callout-5s-001"><ac:rich-text-body>
++<p><strong>Observed behavior:</strong> When the device is offline and the app chains <code>updatePropositions</code> → <code>getPropositions</code> (or <code>getContentCardsUI</code>), cached content may not appear for <strong>up to 5 seconds</strong> — sometimes longer if the update waits on Edge timeout (~10s) first.</p>
++<p><strong>Why it happens today:</strong></p>
++<ul>
++<li><code>getPropositions</code> events are processed on the same <code>eventsQueue</code> as <code>updatePropositions</code> — a get waits behind an in-flight network update.</li>
++<li>Public API uses Event Hub <strong>5s callback timeout</strong> waiting for Messaging to respond.</li>
++<li>Disk hydrate itself is fast (&lt;200ms); the delay is <strong>queue blocking + timeout</strong>, not disk I/O.</li>
++</ul>
++<p><strong>Is 5 seconds acceptable?</strong> <em>Open for product.</em> Proposed mitigation: process read APIs immediately (bypass queue for gets) + integrator cache-first pattern (get before update). Target: sub-second offline render when cache exists.</p>
++</ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h3>6.2 Callout — Memory-first, then persisted storage</h3>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="callout-mem-001"><ac:rich-text-body>
++<p><strong>Proposed read order (all get APIs):</strong></p>
++<ol>
++<li><strong>In-memory cache</strong> — session-qualified propositions from current or prior successful update in this session.</li>
++<li><strong>Disk hydrate</strong> — only when memory is <code>nil</code> or empty for the requested surface; load saved rules, run qualification, populate memory.</li>
++<li><strong>Return</strong> — qualified propositions or empty array (not error).</li>
++</ol>
++<p>No integrator flag. Apps do not choose memory vs disk — SDK decides automatically.</p>
++</ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h3>6.3 Callout — Inbox requires container-item AND cards</h3>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="warning" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="callout-inbox-001"><ac:rich-text-body>
++<p><code>InboxUI.processInboxPropositions</code> needs both the <code>.inbox</code> container-item (layout, capacity, heading) and individual content card propositions. Caching cards alone is insufficient — offline inbox shows error if container-item is missing.</p>
++<p><strong>Validation approach:</strong> Simulation tested persisting cards but not container-item → cold-start offline inbox errors as expected. Final behavior requires both to persist when <code>offlineAvailable</code> is true.</p>
++</ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h3>6.4 Callout — CBE offline caching (proposed)</h3>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="callout-cbe-001"><ac:rich-text-body>
++<p>Code-Based Experiences (<code>.jsonContent</code>, <code>.htmlContent</code>, <code>.defaultContent</code>) follow the same architecture as Content Cards: separate disk key (<code>codeBasedPropositions</code>), same <code>offlineAvailable</code> gate, same memory-first read via <code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code>. Host apps render JSON/HTML from returned proposition <code>data.content</code>.</p>
++</ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h3>6.5 Callout — Dismissed cards on cold start (Option B)</h3>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="note" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="callout-dismiss-001"><ac:rich-text-body>
++<p>Dismiss writes <code>dismiss</code> to Event History; journey rules may later insert <code>disqualify</code>. Until then, a dismissed card may briefly reappear when loaded from disk on cold start. <strong>Option B</strong> (evict from memory + disk on <code>track(.dismiss)</code>) is open — differs from IAM which keeps rules on disk.</p>
++</ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h3>6.6 Callout — InboxUI refresh coupling</h3>
++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="note" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="callout-inbox-refresh-001"><ac:rich-text-body>
++<p>Today <code>InboxUI.performRefresh</code> chains <code>updatePropositions</code> completion → <code>getPropositions</code>. Network failure does not mean propositions are unavailable if disk has data. Once disk hydration ships, this pattern works if get runs after failed update and hydrates. Long-term: consider decoupling refresh (get first, update in background) — same cache-first pattern as Content Cards.</p>
++</ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
++
++<h3>6.7 Open questions summary</h3>
++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
++<tr><th>#</th><th>Question</th><th>Owner</th><th>Status</th></tr>
++<tr><td>OQ-1</td><td>Is 5s offline latency acceptable, or must reads bypass the event queue?</td><td>Product + SDK</td><td>Open</td></tr>
++<tr><td>OQ-2</td><td>Where does authoring place the offline flag? (Options 1–3 in §5.5)</td><td>AJO Product</td><td>Open</td></tr>
++<tr><td>OQ-3</td><td>Should <code>offline</code> default to <code>true</code> or <code>false</code> when absent post-UI launch?</td><td>Product</td><td>Open (currently default <code>true</code>)</td></tr>
++<tr><td>OQ-4</td><td>Option B dismiss disk eviction — ship for CC?</td><td>Product + SDK</td><td>Open</td></tr>
++<tr><td>OQ-5</td><td>Skip persist for empty <code>items[]</code> shells (<a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-64717">PLATIR-64717</a>)?</td><td>SDK</td><td>Open</td></tr>
++<tr><td>OQ-6</td><td>Assurance / analytics event when serving from disk?</td><td>SDK + Product</td><td>Open</td></tr>
++<tr><td>OQ-7</td><td>Public API to clear cached propositions per surface family?</td><td>Product</td><td>Backlog</td></tr>
++<tr><td>OQ-8</td><td>Offline image strategy for CC/CBE media URLs</td><td>Product</td><td>Open (<a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-44800">PLATIR-44800</a>)</td></tr>
++</tbody></table>
++
++<h2>7. Acceptance criteria (product-level)</h2>
++<h3>7.1 User-visible scenarios</h3>
++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
++<tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Expected</th></tr>
++<tr><td>Online update with <code>offline: true</code></td><td>Content visible; eligible rules saved to disk</td></tr>
++<tr><td>Online update with <code>offline: false</code></td><td>Content visible in session; <strong>not</strong> written to disk</td></tr>
++<tr><td>Offline cold start (previously cached)</td><td>Get APIs return cached content (target: &lt;1s after mitigations)</td></tr>
++<tr><td>Offline update attempt</td><td>Update returns <code>success: false</code>; disk unchanged</td></tr>
++<tr><td>Logout → login as different user</td><td>No prior user's CC/CBE/Inbox content</td></tr>
++<tr><td>Inbox offline</td><td>Loads only when container-item + cards both cached</td></tr>
++<tr><td>CBE offline</td><td><code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code> returns JSON/HTML content from disk</td></tr>
++</tbody></table>
++
++<h2>8. Engineering reference (out of PRD scope)</h2>
++<p>File-level implementation, unit tests, and agent guides live in the repository — not duplicated here.</p>
++<ul>
++<li><code>docs/agents/content-card-offline-implementation.md</code> — Content Card offline agent guide</li>
